    "teach_5": {
      "id": "teach_5",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Reverse problems give the final ratio and ask for the original capacity.\n\nIf final wine:water = 16:65, then wine fraction = 16/81.\n\nAfter four equal withdrawals of 8 L from a vessel of x L:\n(x−8)^4 / x^3 = 16x/81 in expanded form, or use (1−8/x)^4 = 16/81.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_5_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_5_step": {
      "id": "teach_5_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Take the fourth root when the fractions are perfect powers.\n\n16/81 = (2/3)^4.\nSo 1−8/x = 2/3.\nThen 8/x = 1/3 → x = 24 L.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_5"
        }
      ]
    },
