        "text": "You can now see why repeated replacement uses multiplication.\n\nEach round keeps a fraction of the original liquid still present, so equal rounds create a power. If the withdrawal changes, multiply the different retention factors instead.\n\nNext, we combine these ideas in multi-ingredient exam puzzles.",
